# Avoid msg.getChat() in whatsapp-web.js

When handling incoming messages in `whatsapp-web.js`, **NEVER** call `await msg.getChat()`. It triggers a flaky Puppeteer DOM evaluation that can crash the agent with `Evaluation failed: r`.

Instead, always identify the chat ID directly from the message object and resolve the human-readable name from the safe memory cache:

```javascript
// 1. Get ID robustly (works for both incoming and outgoing tests)
const chatId = msg.fromMe ? msg.to : msg.from;

// 2. Resolve name from memory cache safely
let chatName = chatId;
try {
  const chats = await client.getChats();
  const targetChat = chats.find(c => c.id._serialized === chatId);
  if (targetChat && targetChat.name) chatName = targetChat.name;
} catch (e) {
  // Safely fallback to raw ID if resolution fails
}
```
